Your rules for this feature, as the builders will follow them (each one applies to every case like it, not just the example):
  1. Whenever a customer asks for their money back before the order ships, cancel the order as a cancellation, not a refund, and return the full amount the customer paid.
  2. Whenever a refund amount works out to a fraction of a rupee, round it down to the whole rupee, so the customer never gets more than they paid.
  3. Whenever a customer returns an item for a reason other than damaged (including 'Other: wrong size') and asks within 14 days of delivery, refund the item prices times quantities, minus the discount code, and do not refund the shipping fee.
  4. Whenever a customer returns an item for a reason other than damaged and asks from day 15 through day 30 after delivery, refund half of the item prices times quantities, minus the discount code, and do not refund the shipping fee.
  5. Whenever a customer returns an item for a reason other than damaged and asks after day 30 after delivery, refund nothing.
  6. Whenever a customer returns an item as damaged and asks up to 90 days after delivery, refund the item prices times quantities, minus the discount code, plus the shipping fee, in place of the amounts that apply to other returns.
  7. Whenever a customer returns an item as damaged and asks after 90 days following delivery, refund nothing.
  8. Whenever a return within 14 days is for a reason other than damaged, refund it to the original payment method: store credit if the order was paid by store credit, or the card if it was paid by card.
  9. Whenever the sales summary is calculated, the Orders count includes every order in the list it is given, including store-credit orders.
  10. Whenever the sales summary is calculated, the Revenue figure includes card orders only, calculated as each card order's item prices times quantities, minus the discount code, plus its shipping fee.
  11. Whenever the sales summary is calculated, orders are not filtered by delivery status or cancellation.
  12. Whenever there are no card orders, the daily summary's average order value is ₹0.
